    "figures": [
        {
            "claim_index": 24,
            "claim": "1. Figure 1: Overview of the Public-Anchor Drift Adapter (PADA) framework. Left: Training phase uses only public Wikipedia text to learn a residual MLP adapter mapping fnew embeddings to fold space via MSE loss. Middle: Deployment phase applies the trained adapter to transform queries for retrieval against the legacy index, without accessing private corpus text. Right: Key insight—embedding drift is model-pair-specific, enabling public anchors to capture the global transform.",
            "verdict": "Verified",
            "explanation": "Analysis stage: The framework description matches the code precisely: (1) wikipedia_anchors.py streams public Wikipedia paragraphs; (2) residual_mlp.py implements ResidualMLPAdapter (g(x) = x + W2*GELU(W1*x+b1)+b2) trained with MSE loss in adapter_trainer.py; (3) retrieval_eval.py applies adapter to transform queries against legacy FAISS index; (4) cross-domain consistency across 4 BEIR domains in all result files confirms the model-pair-specific insight. These architectural facts are directly verified by static code inspection.",
            "evidence": "exp/pada/data/wikipedia_anchors.py; exp/pada/adapters/residual_mlp.py; exp/pada/trainers/adapter_trainer.py; exp/pada/evaluation/retrieval_eval.py; exp/EXPERIMENT_RESULTS/effectiveness_evaluation_report.md",
            "detection_mode": "static_code_analysis",
            "decision_stage": "analysis",
            "analysis_classification": {
                "bucket": "static_verifiable"
            },
            "verification_process": {
                "files_analyzed": [
                    "exp/pada/data/wikipedia_anchors.py",
                    "exp/pada/adapters/residual_mlp.py",
                    "exp/pada/trainers/adapter_trainer.py",
                    "exp/pada/evaluation/retrieval_eval.py",
                    "exp/EXPERIMENT_RESULTS/effectiveness_evaluation_report.md"
                ],
                "commands_executed": []
            }
        },
        {
